warning[needless_bool]: this `if` returns its own condition as a `bool`
  --> tests/lint/needless_bool/bad.jai:4:5
   |
 4 |     if n > 0 return true;
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: write `return n > 0;`
   |
 3   positive :: (n: int) -> bool {
 4 ~     return n > 0;
 5 -     else return false;
 6   }
   |
   = note: `needless_bool` is `warn` by default
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/needless_bool

